<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Tripolitanian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1922 CE · capital Misrata</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Often called the first republic in the Arab world, proclaimed by Tripolitanian leaders in 1918 to resist Italian rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Ottoman defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, Tripolitanian notables met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/msallata">Msallata</a> in November 1918 and proclaimed a republic, exploiting the fact that <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-libya">Italian Libya</a> controlled only the coast. Its leadership was a council including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulayman-al-baruni">Sulayman al-Baruni</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramadan-al-suwayhili">Ramadan al-Suwayhili</a> of Misrata, Ahmad al-Murayyid and Abd al-Nabi Bilkhayr.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic sought international recognition but received none. In 1919 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> issued a statute granting Tripolitanians citizenship and an elected parliament, briefly easing tension. Rivalries among the leaders, between Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> groups and between regions undermined unity; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramadan-al-suwayhili">al-Suwayhili</a> was killed in 1920 during internal fighting.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1922 Tripolitanian leaders offered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> to Idris of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/senussi-order">Senussi Order</a> to unite resistance, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> launched its reconquest the same year, and the republic collapsed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1918 CE – 1922 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.87%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1922 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Misrata</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sulayman al-Baruni, Ramadan al-Suwayhili</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam; Ibadi Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>al-Jumhuriya al-Trabulsiya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=tripolitanian-republic" aria-label="Tripolitanian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5014 995 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tripolitanian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5334 1251L5338 1239"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5338 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5334 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5334 1251h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=tripolitanian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

